# color-role — the semantic color roles: what a color MEANS in an interface, not what it
# looks like. Derived from the Atlassian Design System's color vocabulary: the roles common
# across its text, background, icon, and border aspects. State names (disabled, selected,
# inverse), structural names (accent, input, code), and emphasis names (subtle, subtlest,
# bold) are deliberately excluded — they modify a role; they are not one.

color-role = brand | danger | discovery | information | neutral | success | warning
